      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CANTPLZA MALTEEZA (4) enjoys a class drop off his last attempt in a Breeders Challenge Blue heat at Menangle where he was forced to race three wide without cover. There was merit in his other two efforts this time in including a fourth here two back. Race fit now and this should suit. The recent form of FLO RYDA NZ (1) may not leap off the page but he has had a long string of tough barriers and did come from out wide when he scored at Menangle in September. He is much better served by the ace draw. SHARK DANCER (3) has been coming from tough barriers of late so can do better from a more favourable draw. MADAZALWAYS (9) is another that may require some luck but has claims off back-to-back wins last month.",
